{
  "name": "Monthly GLO/EGM gas-for-crude intercompany tickets",
  "today": "HPLC sells gas to the Texas General Land Office (TGLO) in exchange for crude that EGM receives. To book this correctly, Bryce Baxter set out manual Sitara steps to repeat every month before flash. Someone zeroes the price on the HPLC sale to GLO, enters HPL-to-ENA and ENA-Wellhead demand charges equal to the gas value, and enters an ENA-to-EGM demand charge equal to the prior month's crude value. Julie Meyers did this for January and February 2001. March to May were never done, and O'Neal Winfree put back a price Julie had zeroed. In August, settlements (Megan Parker) had to rebuild the missing months and correct the January and February crude values. By late October, demand fees for earlier months still had to be updated and the August and September crude still had to be booked.",
  "change": "Set up the GLO/EGM intercompany legs as standing deals whose demand charges are calculated each month, with a check before flash, instead of zeroing prices and keying tickets by hand.",
  "explanation": "Book the HPLC-to-GLO sale once at zero price (volume only), so the zero does not have to be redone each month. Make the HPL-to-ENA and ENA-to-EGM legs standing intercompany deals. Each month the gas demand charge is worked out as the firm volume times the published index, which is available shortly after the 1st. The crude demand charge is the prior month's crude value delivered to EGM, entered once by whoever records it. A short check before flash flags any month where a leg is missing or the legs do not net. The scheduler and settlements then only review that check. Months can no longer go undone without anyone noticing, as March to May did, and a hand edit cannot quietly undo the structure.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "547201 & 591307 has been zeroed out.  679847 & 679848 have been created between ENA & HPLC.  679859 has been created for the sale to EGM from ENA Wellhead.  I have placed both January and February on that deal."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Here is a preliminary list of what needs to be done to finish out the transactions for March, April and May."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/28.eml",
      "quote": "I have already sent an email to risk to update the demand fees for the prior months and to book Aug and Sept crude."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "This will require the following steps be taken monthly as this deal goes forward:",
      "note": "The zeroing and the three demand-charge updates are manual steps repeated every month."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "The index for the gas value is available shortly after the 1st of the month, and since the volume is firm, there shouldn't be a problem calculating the value.",
      "note": "The gas leg is a simple calculation from a firm volume and a published index, so it can be calculated automatically."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "she completed January and February, except for one small part, but March forward was never completed.",
      "note": "The hand steps stall. Three months were missed and had to be rebuilt later."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Julie zeroed this out, but O'Neal put it back.",
      "note": "A hand edit undid the monthly zeroing. A standing zero-price setup plus a check would catch or prevent this."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Update Jan and Feb crude values on deal 679859",
      "note": "Even the months that were done needed corrections afterwards, which adds to the cleanup work."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/28.eml",
      "quote": "Below is a summary of where we are on the sale dollars to EGM.  I have already sent an email to risk to update the demand fees for the prior months and to book Aug and Sept crude.",
      "note": "In October 2001 the tickets were still behind and being caught up, so the catch-up work happens more than once."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "month",
    "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
    "quote": "This needs to be done monthly prior to flash"
  },
  "minutes": 80
}

