{
  "name": "Weekly check of ERMS curves against RisktRAC",
  "today": "When a trader starts at a new location, risk management builds the curve in ERMS and then must send a separate request form so Risk Analysis and Reporting sets the same curve up again in RisktRAC, the VaR system. When the form is not sent, the curve exists in ERMS but not in RisktRAC and those positions are left out of VaR. To catch this, Risk Analysis and Reporting began a weekly manual review of new ERMS curves against RisktRAC. The first run found numerous missing curves, and gaps can go unnoticed for up to a week.",
  "change": "A nightly automatic comparison of the ERMS and RisktRAC curve lists replaces the weekly manual review.",
  "explanation": "A scheduled job pulls the curve list from ERMS and from RisktRAC each night and emails Risk Analysis and Reporting, and the risk group that owns the curve, a list of ERMS curves with no RisktRAC match. The same job can also list ERMS books with no matching RisktRAC book. The analyst stops comparing lists by hand each week and only reads the exception email and follows up on what it lists. The request form stays as the way to supply set-up details. Building the missing curves is still done by hand and is not counted in the savings.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/410.eml",
      "quote": "Risk Analysis and Reporting has implemented a new process in which on a weekly basis new curves set up in ERMS are reviewed to ensure that these have been set up in RisktRAC."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/410.eml",
      "quote": "We did this for the first time today and noted numerous curves in ERMS that are not in RisktRAC - which we are working with you to resolve.",
      "note": "The manual review is new and finds many gaps. The gaps can sit unnoticed between weekly reviews."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/410.eml",
      "quote": "If the curve is not set up in RisktRAC the positions are not captured in the VAR or engine, thereby making VAR inaccurate.",
      "note": "This is what a missed set-up costs, and why the check is needed."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/410.eml",
      "quote": "Risk Analysis and Reporting can help, but do not have all of the ERMS information to be able to ensure the completeness of RisktRAC",
      "note": "The analysts doing the review cannot easily see the full ERMS side, so comparing by hand is slow and incomplete. An automatic comparison of the two lists removes this step."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/410.eml",
    "quote": "on a weekly basis new curves set up in ERMS are reviewed"
  },
  "minutes": 40
}

